<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Monzón de Campos</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monzon">Monzón</a> de Campos is a village in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palencia">Palencia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and León, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, on the Carrión in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tierra-de-campos">Tierra de Campos</a>. Its castle was the seat of the County of Monzón, created around 943 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramiro-ii-of-leon">Ramiro II of León</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assur-fernandez">Assur Fernández</a> and ruled by the Ansúrez family. The county was later absorbed into the kingdoms of León and Castile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/monzon-de-campos.jpg" alt="Monzón de Campos" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Luis Rogelio HM · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monzon_de_Campos_-_006_(39299858320).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
